  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nThe current approach struggles with optimization due to three primary bottlenecks:\n1) High dimensionality (280+ samples)\n2) Poor exploration due to local optimization\n3) FFT bottleneck in correlation calculation\n\nThe proposed approach tackles these by:\n1) Using sparse representation with Hermite interpolation that leverages moments\n2) Exploiting functional properties rather than grid points\n3) Using cascading from lower resolutions to capture optimal structure\n4) Context was maintained across resolutions via derivative transfers\n\nWhile maintaining mathematical equivalence, the sparse representation reduces computational burden by orders of magnitude. The Hermite method computes moments analytically and maintains integral constraints automatically through basis projection.\n\nMathematical specification:\nThe transformation from grid function h(x) to moment vector m_j and vice versa preserves all function properties needed:\n- h(x) \u2208 [0,1] \u27fa m_j satisfies certain inequalities\n- \u222bh(x)dx = 0.5 remains integral constraint\n- The correlation calculation becomes \u03a3h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx \u2192 \u2211m_i,m_j[terms with shifts]\n\nThe objective transforms into:\nC_5 = (2/n) \u00d7 max_k |<\u03c8_k, m>| where \u03c8_k =\u27e81-h(x+k)\u27e9\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Start from parent grid (n=280) interpolation\n2. Transform grid samples \u2192 moment vector using:\n   m_j = (2/n)^j * \u222b\u2080\u00b2 x^j h(x)dx\n3. Perform optimization in moment space using:\n   - Analytical derivatives for correlations\n   - Moment projection enforcing [0,1] constraints\n   - Rescale and convert back to grid via Hermite series\n4. Verify constraint: \u03a3m_j where j\u22650 should imply \u222bh(x)dx=0.5\n5. Evaluate using: grid_copy = hermite_to_grid(m, n)\n\nSearch choices:\nGrid: 280\u2192560\u21921120 doubling path\nTemperature: slow exponential decay for annealing\nCooling: 1000\u219250\u219210 schedule scaled by grid\nRMSE between cascaded grids was used as fitness metric\n\nBudget and robustness:\n- Phase 0: Moment space optimization (600s)\n- Phase 1: Grid doubling (300s each)\n- Handle projector for invalid states\n- Use grid fallback if optimization diverges\n\nValidation contract:\nMust pass:\n1) np.isin(h[i], [0,1]).all() approximately\n2) np.sum(h.clip(0,1).round(10)) \u2248 n/2\n3) np.max(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\")) * dx\nSimilar to original eval",
